Torne ke baad sirf yeh chand integrals kaam aate hain, inhein achhi tarah yaad kar lein:
\(\int \frac{dx}{x - a} = \ln|x - a| + c\) aur \(\int \frac{dx}{ax + b} = \frac{1}{a}\ln|ax + b| + c\) (\(\frac{1}{a}\) is liye ke \(ax + b\) ka derivative \(a\) hai);
\(\int \frac{dx}{(x - a)^n} = \frac{(x - a)^{1-n}}{1 - n} + c\), jab \(n \ne 1\) (yani squared ya us se zyada power par \(\ln\) nahi, power rule);
\(\int \frac{2x}{x^2 + a^2}\,dx = \ln(x^2 + a^2) + c\) (numerator denominator ka derivative hai);
\(\int \frac{dx}{x^2 + a^2} = \frac{1}{a}\tan^{-1}\frac{x}{a} + c\).
Constants dhoondne ka tareeqa: pehle linear factors ke roots rakhein (har root ek ke ilawa sab terms mita deta hai); jab koi root na bache to \(x\) ki powers ke coefficients compare karein (yani dono taraf \(x^2\) ke saath wala number barabar, \(x\) ke saath wala barabar, waghera).
